Template:Align/Doc.text:
This is a helper template that aligns its content in the centre, if the align parameter is set accordingly. This shouldn't be used in writing articles; its use is to avoid repeating substantial parts of templates when implementing conditional alignment.

{{align|align=center|Some content}}

=== Usage ===

In a template, wrap the content you want to conditionally align within this template, and forward the align argument:

{{code|lang=mediawiki|line=no|<nowiki>{{align|align={{{align|}}}|...}}</nowiki>}}
<includeonly>
=== Template data ===

<templatedata>
{
  "description": "Helper template to conditionally align content in the centre. Do not use in usual articles.",
  "params": {
    "1": {
      "label": "Content",
      "description": "The content to be aligned",
      "type": "content",
      "required": true
    },
    "align": {
      "label": "Alignment",
      "description": "The alignment of the content. Any values other than 'center' have no effect.",
      "type": "string",
      "suggested": true,
      "suggestedvalues": [
        "center",
        "left",
        "right"
      ]
    }
  }
}
</templatedata>
</includeonly>

Template:Archive/Doc.text:
This template is used to mark articles that are original works that are preserved for their enciclopaedic value, '''with the authors' consent'''. This template is '''never''' to be used as justification for copy-pasting original work, nor is it to be used for advertising purposes.

{{archive|category=no|original=https://www.nix.dev}}

=== Usage ===

Once you have the '''express permission''' of the original authors, you may include this template along with its original source like so:

{{code|lang=mediawiki|line=no|<nowiki>{{archive|original=https://www.nix.dev}}</nowiki>}}

Template:Aside/Doc.text:
This is a template for displaying related information, that is not essential to the main body of the article.

{{aside|Templates are generally useful for reusing bits of code across different pages, as well as standardising formatting across the wiki.}}

=== Usage ===

You can simply include this template alongside a message to display. The notice above can be replicated as such:

{{bc|<nowiki>{{aside|Templates are generally useful for reusing bits of code across different pages, as well as standardising formatting across the wiki.}}</nowiki>}}

You can also customise the ''"Sidenote"'' text:

{{bc|<nowiki>{{aside|leading=For your information:|You can change the leading text}}</nowiki>}}

{{aside|leading=For your information:|You can change the leading text}}

Template:Box/Doc.text:
This template is used to generate boxes that can hold content. In particular, boxes are used for [[Template:Notice|notices]]. An example of a box holding content:

{{Box|This is a box with some text content}}

===Usage===

Simply feed in your content as the first argument to the template:

{{code|lang=mediawiki|line=no|<nowiki>{{Box|This is a box with some text content}}</nowiki>}}

If you need content that is styled via MediaWiki syntax, you might need to place your content on a new line. You can also set the <code>wikiContent</code> argument in order to adjust the padding of the box to fit the content in a more visually appealing manner:

{{code|lang=mediawiki|line=no|<nowiki>
{{Box|wikiContent=yes|
== Heading ==
Some content
}}
</nowiki>}}

{{Box|wikiContent=yes|
==Heading==
Some content
}}

