Template:Copypaste/Doc.text:
Use this template to mark an article or section that may have been copied and pasted from an original source, possibly marking a copyright violation. This template automatically adds the article to a [[:Category:Copypasted articles|list of articles]] with potential copyright violation.

{{copypaste|category=no}}

=== Usage ===

You can simply include this template in the article or section it should apply to:

{{code|lang=mediawiki|line=no|<nowiki>{{copypaste}}</nowiki>}}

Template:Delete/Doc.text:
When a page is not significant enough to be a standalone article, or when the information on it is no longer relevant, a page may be proposed for deletion. In that case, use this template to mark it. This will automatically categorise it under the [[:Category:Deletion candidates|list of deletion candidates]]. The notice includes a link to the page's talk page, where editors can weigh in on the proposal, bringing arguments for and against its deletion.

{{delete|category=no}}

=== Usage ===

Include the template along with a reason for the deletion on the page you want to propose for deletion:

{{bc|<nowiki>{{delete|reason=This page is about space monkeys, not about NixOS.}}</nowiki>}}

{{delete|category=no|reason=This page is about space monkeys, not about NixOS.}}

Template:Disambiguation/Doc.text:
Sometimes a single word or phrase can be used to refer to many different things. In these cases we might need to differentiate between different terms using this template.

{{Disambiguation|category=no|Template:Notice}}

=== Usage ===

It is simply sufficient to include this template, along with the name of the page that sounds similar. The notice above can be crafted by:

{{bc|<nowiki>{{Disambiguation|Template:Notice}}</nowiki>}}

If the disambiguation is particularly complex, you might need to override the message altogether:

{{bc|<nowiki>{{Disambiguation|message=This refers to the disambiguation template. For a notice see [[Template:Notice]], and for a note see [[Template:Note]]}}</nowiki>}}

{{Disambiguation|category=no|message=This refers to the disambiguation template. For a notice see [[Template:Notice]], and for a note see [[Template:Note]]}}

Template:Expand/Doc.text:
This template can be used to mark an article or section that is incomplete, needlessly succinct, or that needs more information to be added. Editors are encouraged to regularly check the [[:Category:Articles that need expanding|list of articles that need to be expanded]] and contribute by adding more information to them.

{{expand|category=no}}

=== Usage ===

One can simply include this template in a page to produce a notice like the one above:

{{code|lang=mediawiki|line=no|<nowiki>{{expand}}</nowiki>}}

You can also include a reason for the notice, as well as the scope of the information to be expanded. For example, a notice that specifies this template needs expanding because there are features that can be added would look like this:

{{code|lang=mediawiki|line=no|<nowiki>{{expand|scope=template|There are new features that can be added.}}</nowiki>}}

{{Expansion|category=no|scope=template|There are new features that can be added.}}

