This template is used to group together a number of user badges on a user's page.

{{user badge dock|{{user badge/wikiproject popular boards|category=no}}{{user badge/wikiproject mobile|category=no}}{{user badge/wikiproject templates|category=no}}}}

=== Usage ===

Simply include the ''specific [[Template:user badge|user badges]]'' you want as the first argument to this template:

{{code|lang=mediawiki|line=no|<nowiki>
{{user badge dock|{{user badge/wikiproject popular boards}}{{user badge/wikiproject mobile}}{{user badge/wikiproject templates}}}}</nowiki>}}

Template:User badge/Doc.text:
This template is used to display user badges. This is a ''fun'' functionality to allow users to display information about their wiki activity, such as belonging to a specific [[NixOS Wiki:WikiProjects|WikiProject]]. This template shouldn't be used directly, it should be used in sub-templates created as sub-pages to this template. For example, {{tl|user badge/wikiproject popular boards}}.

{{user badge|icon=♥|color=var(--color-error)|background=var(--background-color-error-subtle)|Template lover|This user loves [[Help:Templates|Templates]]}}

=== Usage ===

Include '''the specific badge''' you want into [[Special:YourPage|your user page]]. For example:

{{code|lang=mediawiki|line=no|<nowiki>{{user badge/wikiproject popular boards}}</nowiki>}}

{{user badge/wikiproject popular boards|category=no}}

Template:Wip/Doc.text:
If you need more time to bring an article or section up to the wiki's standards, you may use this template '''for a limited amount of time.''' Ideally, remove it as soon as possible, preferably within a week from the start of the work. You don't need it if your work is in your [[Help:Sandbox|own sandbox]], or if the edits are self-contained and don't affect the readability of the article.

Editors are encouraged to regularly check the [[:Category:Works in progress|list of WIP articles]], and prompt the original author to finish their work and remove the notice.

{{wip|category=no}}

=== Usage ===

Simply include the template at the top of the article or section you are working on, along with the date on which the work started

{{code|lang=wiki|line=no|<nowiki>{{wip|date=1 July 1980}}</nowiki>}}

You can also specify more information about your work and the scope:

{{code|lang=wiki|line=no|<nowiki>{{wip|date=1 July 1980|scope=template|reason=Implementing VR rendering.}}</nowiki>}}

{{wip|category=no|date=1 July 1980|scope=template|reason=Implementing VR rendering.}}
